[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3 uid="uid://unitarraymeshcompscene"]

; The same textured quad as unit-arraymesh-uv.tscn, its .tres surface stored with
; ARRAY_FLAG_COMPRESS_ATTRIBUTES — positions as uint16 spanning the surface aabb, the
; tangent frame as an axis-angle pair plus an angle, UVs as uint16. That flag is the ONE
; variable: same four vertices, same aabb, same normals, same UVs, same material, same
; transform, so this image must be indistinguishable from unit-arraymesh-uv.tscn's.
; Every other fixture .tres in the bag is uncompressed, so no other scene reads a single
; byte of the compressed layout, and the corpus meshes that do are not visual-gated. A
; wrong position stride renders nothing at all, a normal read off the rotation axis
; instead of through the axis-angle frame lights the quad from the wrong side, and a UV
; read at the wrong width scrambles the bands.

[ext_resource type="ArrayMesh" path="res://unit-arraymesh-compressed-quad.tres" id="1_quad"]

